<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<addon
  id="inputstream.tempo"
  version="22.4.1"
  name="Inputstream Tempo"
  provider-name="kontell">
  <requires>@ADDON_DEPENDS@</requires>
  <extension
    point="kodi.inputstream"
    name="tempo"
    extension=""
    tags="true"
    listitemprops="program_number|stream_mode|open_mode|manifest_type|default_url|is_realtime_stream|playback_as_live|programme_start_time|programme_end_time|catchup_url_format_string|catchup_url_near_live_format_string|catchup_buffer_start_time|catchup_buffer_end_time|catchup_buffer_offset|catchup_terminates|catchup_granularity|timezone_shift|default_programme_duration|programme_catchup_id|tempo|tempo_file|start_time|queue_secs|lead_secs"
    library_@PLATFORM@="@LIBRARY_FILENAME@" />
  <extension point="xbmc.service" library="resources/lib/runner.py"/>
  <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
    <platform>@PLATFORM@</platform>
    <license>GPL-2.0-or-later</license>
    <summary lang="en_GB">InputStream client with tempo control (pitch-corrected playback speed) for audio and video</summary>
    <description lang="en_GB">InputStream client based on FFmpeg with built-in tempo processing. Supports pitch-corrected playback speed from 0.5x to 100x for audiobooks and podcasts, and rate-shifts video and subtitles in step with the audio so the same control works for video. Based on inputstream.ffmpegdirect.</description>
    <news>v22.4.1 Seeks keep the first packets of the new position: the probe for where a seek landed used to read and free them, so decoders started mid-GOP after every seek (HEVC logged it, a Pixel 7 AV1 decoder wedged on it). v22.4.0 Tempo now covers video: video and subtitle packets are projected through the same content/output time map as the stretched audio, so a video item plays in sync at any rate. Seeks, the OSD and external subtitles follow the map (IPOSTIME is advertised for video items); the audio pipeline follows Kodi's audio-track selection; time is reported at the playing point given the queue depth (queue_secs); tempo changes are polled by wall clock and written back to tempo_file.state; HDR colour metadata is now passed through.</news>
  </extension>
</addon>
